WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.234
Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.036
made his first public appearance

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.070
on the global stage

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.206
since that Wagner rebellion

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.140
late last month.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.775
Vladimir Putin appearing alongside

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.043
other international leaders,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:10.877
including Chinese

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.012
President Xi Jinping,

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.513
in a virtual summit.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.147
CNN's Will

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.415
Ripley is covering this story

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.416
from Taiwan.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:16.950
So, Will,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.687
what was the Russian president's message

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:21.988
it was

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.523
it was the optics of the whole thing

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.824
that was particularly interesting

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.027
to see Putin and Xi.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:27.794
These two,

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.963
you know, no limits partners

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.865
at a time that Putin's power

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.299
is very much in question

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.801
after what happened in late

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.002
June with the Wagner group.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.837
And then, of course, President Xi,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.072
who is arguably stronger

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:39.572
than ever,

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.273
really assuming

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.474
his role of the leader

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.410
of the authoritarian bloc,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.078
if you will, which also includes

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.946
Belarus and Iran, would join

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.148
this Shanghai

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.482
cooperation organization meeting,

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.850
which was hosted online

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.085
by the Indian prime minister.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.354
And so Putin, in his message, talked

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.089
about deeper

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.223
security cooperation

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.259
between the members of this organization,

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.027
and he insisted that Moscow

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:01.895
would stand up against

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:02.495
what he called

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.531
illegitimate sanctions

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.933
over his unprovoked invasion of Ukraine.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:07.333
Listen,

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.003
But I

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.538
see the Russian people

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.773
are consolidated as never before.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.607
The solidarity

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.742
and high responsibility

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.077
for the fate of the Fatherland

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.511
was clearly demonstrated

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.280
by Russian political circles

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.614
and the entire society

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:22.348
by coming out

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:23.450
as a united front

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.919
against the attempted armed rebellion

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:26.920
revolution

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:30.890
Obviously, Putin there

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.759
with a lot of friendly leaders.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:33.660
This is this is

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.994
this was not a contentious

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:35.695
group of people

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.163
that were going to try to go after him

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.566
or embarrass him in this first

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.267
multilateral international

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.068
forum appearance

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.503
since those armed mercenaries

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.572
threatened to march on Moscow.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.440
But he did express appreciation

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.541
to the leaders for their support,

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.677
including China's Xi Jinping Xi.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.845
For his part,

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.647
he called out kind of in an indirect way.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.583
Alex, the United States

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:57.217
saying that

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.585
the world should reject what he called

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.353
protectionism and decoupling.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.054
This is a reference,

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.555
of course, to the United States

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.623
efforts to try to reduce

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.357
trade and investment

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.291
with China, particularly

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.159
in sensitive areas

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.961
such as technology, which the U.S.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.062
has long feared is being

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.430
used by the Chinese military.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.800
All right, Will Ripley in Taipei,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.968
thank you very much.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.069
Let's go straight to our experts

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.070
to break all this down.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:17.971
Our military analyst,

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.339
the retired Lieutenant General

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.940
Mark Hertling, and Jill Dougherty,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.509
who, of course, is a CNN contributor

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.343
on Russian affairs.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:23.743
Thank you

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:24.911
both for joining me

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.779
on this Fourth of July.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.448
Jill, I want to start with you.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.282
How important

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.049
is it

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:30.783
right now

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.052
for Putin to appear on this global stage

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.089
surrounded by big global leaders

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:39.159
like those of China and India?

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.393
Oh, I think it's crucial

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.861
because after all, you know, a

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.931
week or so ago, you had a rebellion

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.166
with troops

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.568
or fighters on their way to Moscow.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.869
That undermines

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.504
Putin's image

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.705
not only domestically,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.940
but internationally.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.441
And a lot of these countries

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.677
that have supported him

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.778
must be asking

00:02:58.778 --> 00:02:59.412
the question,

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.381
is he really still in charge?

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.982
Is he still,

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:03.449
you know,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.418
Vladimir Putin, who we supported

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:05.752
said or

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.921
a lot of questioning behind the scenes

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.557
and he absolutely had to get out there.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.091
He's been out domestically

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.860
and now internationally.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.262
General Hertling,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:16.696
we just

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.363
heard today

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:18.531
that the NATO's secretary

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.766
general, Jens Stoltenberg,

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.801
his term has been extended

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.470
by another year.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:25.939
What do you think

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.941
allies need to accomplish

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.877
in this upcoming NATO's summit in Vilnius

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.780
as it pertains to Ukraine?

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.215
Yeah, well, first of all, access

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:35.848
a great point,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:36.916
because Secretary

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:37.684
Sullivan said

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:40.687
the mayor has selflessly done this.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:43.122
He wanted to retire long ago.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.157
He stayed on

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.525
because he realizes

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:48.928
that NATO's is at war in all effects.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.697
So what he will

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.098
accomplish is a continual

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.199
coordination

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.835
of the alliance to support Ukraine.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.037
It's an important point.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.539
He is very selfless

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.007
and doing it, as I just said,

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.042
and it's a good thing.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.912
There will be several things

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.513
that he will accomplish.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.616
Being familiar with the situation

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.618
and certainly linked with

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:13.753
Defense Minister Reznik call from Ukraine

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.488
and certainly Defense Minister

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.056
or minister of defense

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.425
excuse me, Secretary of Defense

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.527
Austin and Secretary of State Blinken

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.528
from the United States.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:24.230
There

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.298
are, of course, Jill

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.400
real divisions among NATO's leaders

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.137
about how when, if Ukraine should join

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.772
the Naito Alliance.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:35.241
How much do you think NATO's is weighing

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.011
Russia's opposition to the expansion

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.212
of NATO's

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:42.148
and how Putin may respond to that?

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.950
Oh, I think less than ever.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.219
I mean, that used to be the debate.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.688
You know, will this anger Putin?

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:51.624
There's a lot of the reverse feeling now.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.326
I mean, what you hear from the allies,

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.861
especially the ones that are saying

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:55.795
the Baltics

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.130
and Poland, etc.,

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.531
are saying we don't care

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.832
what Putin thinks.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:00.600
In fact,

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.969
if we continue to think about why Putin

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.370
what Putin thinks

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.572
we will weaken our own defense.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.708
So it's really full steam ahead.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:09.709
The problem,

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:10.443
I think,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.045
is the United States

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:13.946
and some other countries are a little bit

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.481
more careful about it.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.550
And the trick would be trying

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.451
to figure out

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.086
what can you give Ukraine

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:20.887
to give them hope

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:21.921
that there will be something

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:22.789
in the future

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.824
without committing Entirely.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:26.492
That's really difficult balance

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.760
that that's what they'll be working.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:29.796
And of course, so much has

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:30.229
been given

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:30.897
to Ukraine

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:32.298
ahead of this counteroffensive,

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:34.067
both in terms of training

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.668
and in terms of weaponry.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:36.936
General Hertling,

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.905
are you seeing signs that

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:41.174
that Ukraine is gaining momentum

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:42.175
in this counteroffensive?

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:42.942
They have taken,

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:43.609
I think some

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.645
14, 15 square miles,

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:47.880
but really have yet to punch through.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.648
How much progress

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:50.283
do you think they're making?

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.951
I am seeing momentum, Alex,

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:52.952
and it's a great question

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:54.721
because there's a lot of Western analysts

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:55.955
who suggest that Ukraine

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:57.690
is not going fast enough.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.359
One of the things I'd point out

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:02.261
is Ukraine is now the third largest army

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:02.762
in Europe.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:04.831
Behind Russia and Turkey,

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.699
that they were at one point

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.868
about the 11th largest army in Europe.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:11.137
So we're talking about the capability

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:11.904
of the Ukrainian

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.005
armed forces

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.708
to become even stronger on a daily basis.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:19.112
And what I see is they are conducting

00:06:19.112 --> 00:06:21.214
this operation in a very

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.016
very correct manner.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.051
They're probing.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:25.818
They're continuing

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.387
to look for ways to assault.

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:28.988
They're keeping their reserves there.

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:29.822
Nine brigades

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:30.456
that have been trained

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.325
in the rest in the West

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:34.193
excuse me, in reserve

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.862
so they can conduct the operation

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:37.730
once they find the weak spots

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.031
in the Russian lines.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.566
It's going to be a very tough fight

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.902
in the next six to eight weeks.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.670
But I think Ukraine is going to succeed

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.872
in what they're doing.

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:46.038
You know,

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:46.773
a very tough fight

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:47.907
could take quite some time.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:48.541
Jill Dougherty,

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.642
Lieutenant General Mark Hertling,

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.476
thank you both for joining me.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.812
A very happy fourth of July to you both

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:54.147
and to you. Thank you.

